  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 PM MDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nLight precipitation will continue to fall across the east and \nsoutheast highlands through late tonight, where another few \nhundredths to 0.20\" of liquid accumulation is forecast.\nLight snow or rain/snow mix remains likely for the highest \nelevations.\n\nThe coldest timeframe of the forecast period will be tomorrow \nmorning as clouds clear and temperatures drop into the mid- to upper \n20s. Freeze Warnings are in effect from 3 AM and 9 AM Wednesday for \nall five of our growing zones. This will likely mark an end to the \ngrowing season. Another impact we may contend with Wednesday morning \nis areas of dense fog forming behind clearing skies late tonight.\n\nDaytime temperatures will continue to warm through the duration of \nthe extended period as high pressure builds over the region from the \nwest. Temperatures today will again run +/- 15 degrees below normal \nwith widespread 40s, warming into the 60s by late week. Conditions \nwill also remain dry through the weekend.\n\nEnsembles show the next trough moving onshore early next week with \nNational Blend high temperatures dropping 10 to 15 degrees between \nMonday and Tuesday.",
